WEBVTT

00:01.160 --> 00:04.070
Get ready to turn your
brains to viewing mode

00:04.100 --> 00:05.600
because, previously
on "Final Space,"

00:05.630 --> 00:06.870
Gary just received
a Mayday call

00:06.900 --> 00:09.540
for none other than Quinn,
the super-spicy captain

00:09.570 --> 00:12.510
he hasn't stopped thinking
about for the past five years.

00:12.540 --> 00:14.380
What a loser!
Ha ha ha!

00:14.410 --> 00:16.710
Oh, and Quinn is on the run
from the Infinity Guard?

00:16.750 --> 00:21.680
Whoa! We've had our fun.
Get ready to have yours.

00:22.390 --> 00:27.120
♪♪

00:27.160 --> 00:29.490
H.U.E.: Gary, you have
six minutes

00:29.530 --> 00:31.060
of oxygen left.

00:32.560 --> 00:35.130
Gary: It can't be.

00:35.160 --> 00:36.800
What are you doing, Gary?

00:36.830 --> 00:38.730
What do you think I'm doing?
I'm gonna consume its power.

00:38.770 --> 00:41.440
But opening your helmet
will blow out your internals,

00:41.470 --> 00:43.370
inducing
instantaneous death.

00:43.410 --> 00:45.210
That's one
possible outcome.

00:45.240 --> 00:47.710
Another, I eat the cookie,
and its power turns me

00:47.740 --> 00:49.750
into a majestic
space-breathing manticore.

00:49.780 --> 00:52.320
You will die before
you eat the cookie.

00:52.350 --> 00:55.180
I'm pretty sure I could get it
in there before I die.

00:55.220 --> 00:58.350
-That is not possible, Gary.
-I really think I can do it.

00:58.390 --> 01:01.560
I'm gonna lob it right in
and close the helmet super fast.

01:01.590 --> 01:02.530
You can't, Gary.

01:02.560 --> 01:06.630
No lobbing,
no closing, no cookie.

01:06.660 --> 01:09.700
[ Sighs ]

01:09.730 --> 01:19.740
♪♪

01:19.780 --> 01:29.750
♪♪

01:29.790 --> 01:35.720
♪♪

01:35.760 --> 01:41.630
♪♪

01:41.660 --> 01:43.530
Quinn: Mayday, Mayday!

01:43.570 --> 01:46.140
My name is Quinn Airgone,
a captain in the Infinity Guard.

01:46.170 --> 01:48.300
I've been investigating
a gravitational disturbance,

01:48.340 --> 01:50.440
which I now see
is a breach in space.

01:50.470 --> 01:55.440
Many people are dead, and I'm
about to join them unless...

01:55.480 --> 01:59.580
Aah! Is there not a single idiot
that can hear me?!

01:59.620 --> 02:03.150
I can hear her.

02:03.190 --> 02:05.920
The greatest love story
in the history of the universe

02:05.950 --> 02:07.620
is about to blossom forth.

02:07.660 --> 02:10.460
Yo, dude, just keep
the expectations in check.

02:10.490 --> 02:12.630
Quinn hasn't responded
to a single message of yours

02:12.660 --> 02:13.830
in five years.

02:13.860 --> 02:15.830
People get busy.
I'm busy.

02:15.860 --> 02:16.930
For five years?

02:16.970 --> 02:20.170
4 years, 11 months
and 30 days.

02:20.200 --> 02:22.310
-That's five years, bro.
-Maybe it is. Maybe it isn't.

02:22.340 --> 02:24.410
-It is.
-But it could not be.

02:24.440 --> 02:26.940
H.U.E.: Disabled transporter
is now locked in.

02:26.980 --> 02:29.380
Dispatching Sames
to secure Quinn.

02:29.410 --> 02:30.850
Over my hard nipples,
H.U.E.!

02:30.880 --> 02:33.320
If anyone is saving Quinn,
it's me, the captain.

02:33.350 --> 02:37.350
Gary, for what is
the 9,045th time,

02:37.390 --> 02:39.490
you are still a prisoner.
-I disagree.

02:39.520 --> 02:41.890
As soon as the crap
hit the interstellar fan,

02:41.920 --> 02:43.660
I became the captain
for real.

02:43.690 --> 02:45.330
Calculating, no.

02:45.360 --> 02:46.760
Calculating, yes.

02:46.800 --> 02:49.830
I will use those powers
to rescue Quinn.

02:49.870 --> 02:52.340
One week has been added
to your sentence.

02:52.370 --> 02:53.970
Frickin' what -- what --
w-- what's new, H.U.E.?

02:54.000 --> 02:55.670
What's new?

02:55.700 --> 02:57.840
Now, before I risk my life
for the woman I love,

02:57.870 --> 02:59.840
does anyone perchance
have a breath mint?

02:59.880 --> 03:02.410
-Right here, Gary.
-Ach! Oh!

03:02.450 --> 03:04.350
God, no, I'm killing
my best friend!

03:04.380 --> 03:06.280
Let KVN get it.
I can do it.

03:06.320 --> 03:08.220
I'm close.
It's right there.

03:08.250 --> 03:11.590
Whoa, KVN, stay away,
far away from me forever!

03:11.620 --> 03:13.720
Oh, my God! Ugh!

03:13.760 --> 03:19.460
♪♪

03:19.500 --> 03:21.860
Aah!

03:21.900 --> 03:26.570
♪♪

03:26.600 --> 03:29.810
[ Beeping ]

03:29.840 --> 03:32.840
Gary: Commencing rescue.
Commencing destiny.

03:32.880 --> 03:42.720
♪♪

03:42.750 --> 03:53.560
♪♪

03:53.600 --> 04:03.570
♪♪

04:03.610 --> 04:13.480
♪♪

04:13.520 --> 04:15.320
♪♪

04:15.350 --> 04:17.990
Nice work. I need
to commandeer your ship.

04:18.020 --> 04:19.790
I have
a class-three priority.

04:19.820 --> 04:23.360
Quinn, you look
every bit as spicy

04:23.390 --> 04:26.060
as the last time
I saw you.

04:26.090 --> 04:28.560
Great,
and you are again?

04:28.600 --> 04:29.930
Oh-ho-ho!

04:29.970 --> 04:32.070
How I've missed
your razor-sharp wit.

04:32.100 --> 04:34.300
No, seriously, I have
no idea who you are.

04:34.340 --> 04:35.700
Really?

04:35.740 --> 04:37.910
You resemble no one
I know, so, yeah, really.

04:37.940 --> 04:39.540
-Seriously?
-Seriously.

04:39.580 --> 04:41.540
Oh, dear Lord, you're
suffering from amnesia!

04:41.580 --> 04:43.950
I'm suffering
from an emergency

04:43.980 --> 04:46.480
that's going
to destroy Earth.

04:46.520 --> 04:48.920
[ Laughs ] Quinn, you really
expect me to believe

04:48.950 --> 04:50.090
you don't know who I am?

04:50.120 --> 04:52.560
Hold on.
I know how to fix this.

04:52.590 --> 04:56.790
[ Smacks lips ]
This is the real raw Gary.

04:56.830 --> 04:58.930
[ Laughs ] That didn't fix it,
whoever you are.

04:58.960 --> 05:00.960
What a dagger
to the heart.

05:01.000 --> 05:03.370
I'm the guy who,
for the past five years,

05:03.400 --> 05:04.800
has been sending
daily documentaries

05:04.830 --> 05:08.640
to the woman
who has no idea who I am!

05:08.670 --> 05:11.710
Wow, that sucks.
I never got any of them.

05:11.740 --> 05:14.340
Now, if you could just show me
where the bridge is...

05:14.380 --> 05:17.410
It's all good.
Life, you know?

05:17.450 --> 05:21.950
Hmm, cute guy, but issues,
definite issues.

05:21.980 --> 05:23.750
[ Crying ]

05:23.790 --> 05:25.850
Quinn doesn't
even know who I am!

05:25.890 --> 05:28.590
Oh, no! Oh!

05:28.620 --> 05:30.730
Oh! Uh!

05:30.760 --> 05:35.130
Oh, this is not what
it's supposed to be.

05:35.160 --> 05:38.130
Oh, God, it hurts so much!

05:38.170 --> 05:41.570
Oh, she doesn't
even know who I am!

05:41.600 --> 05:44.010
I need to record my feelings!

05:44.040 --> 05:45.740
Quinn, for future reference,

05:45.770 --> 05:48.080
the decent thing would've
been to fake amnesia.

05:48.110 --> 05:49.780
I would've faked amnesia.

05:49.810 --> 05:51.450
People I know and love
all would've faked amnesia,

05:51.480 --> 05:52.720
but you had to be honest.

05:52.750 --> 05:54.150
Name one decent relationship

05:54.180 --> 05:55.820
that has ever been
built on honesty.

05:55.850 --> 05:57.620
You can't, can you?

05:57.650 --> 05:59.590
That's because there aren't any.

06:01.920 --> 06:03.630
I know this doesn't
make any sense,

06:03.660 --> 06:05.830
but I really needed to talk
to somebody right now,

06:05.860 --> 06:07.760
and you're the only person
I can open my heart wallet to

06:07.800 --> 06:09.700
and spend
my hurt coins with.

06:09.730 --> 06:12.000
-Jerry?
-Oh! Jerry?

06:12.030 --> 06:15.000
You don't even
know my name.

06:15.040 --> 06:16.070
Avocato,
is he all right?

06:16.100 --> 06:18.570
-No.
-You know Avocato's name?

06:18.610 --> 06:21.780
-Hey, gang.
-Not now, KVN.

06:21.810 --> 06:23.580
Carl, Hank,
Orson, Noodles,

06:23.610 --> 06:25.180
can you give me
and, uh...

06:25.210 --> 06:27.820
-Gary.
-...Gary a minute?

06:29.220 --> 06:30.890
Who are you
recording that for?

06:30.920 --> 06:32.920
Someone who meant
quite a lot to me.

06:32.960 --> 06:34.720
I hope she gets
to see it one day.

06:34.760 --> 06:36.060
When you're this
far out in space,

06:36.090 --> 06:38.790
most of that stuff
gets lost.

06:38.830 --> 06:40.130
Suppose it does.

06:40.160 --> 06:41.960
What did you
come here for?

06:42.000 --> 06:45.200
I just wanted to say,
"Thank you, Gerald."

06:45.230 --> 06:46.600
You're welcome.

06:46.640 --> 06:48.100
Gerald?
Is his name Gerald?

06:48.140 --> 06:50.070
Was he lying to us
this whole time?

06:50.110 --> 06:52.640
I'm confused.
Maybe Gerald is a nickname.

06:52.680 --> 06:54.080
Maybe his last name
is Gerald.

06:54.110 --> 06:57.510
Help me to understand,
Gerald, Gary, Gerald.

07:04.120 --> 07:06.220
SAMES:
This ship has been seized

07:06.250 --> 07:08.920
by the authority
of the Infinity Guard.

07:13.530 --> 07:16.570
Carl, not right now.
I've had a bad day.

07:16.600 --> 07:18.570
I am really not in the mood
for a hug, Carl.

07:18.600 --> 07:21.070
Carl, that's enough.
I'm fine. Get away from me!

07:21.100 --> 07:23.070
Bad Carl! Bad Carl!

07:23.110 --> 07:25.470
Bad Carl!

07:25.510 --> 07:26.880
H.U.E. Emergency.

07:26.910 --> 07:29.210
Our power reactor
has been drained.

07:29.240 --> 07:32.150
The Galaxy I is immobilized.

07:35.980 --> 07:39.120
A takeover command has been
uploaded into my system.

07:39.150 --> 07:41.760
I am fighting it,
but it will succeed.

07:41.790 --> 07:43.630
Okay. Uh.

07:43.660 --> 07:45.690
It's the Infinity Guard.
We've been hacked.

07:45.730 --> 07:47.200
For some reason,
they're trying

07:47.230 --> 07:48.900
to shut down
my investigation.

07:48.930 --> 07:50.970
-What a bunch of nerds.
-They're after me.

07:51.000 --> 07:53.670
-You? Why? You're perfect.
-Where do I start?

07:53.700 --> 07:55.070
The Earth is being sucked
into a black hole.

07:55.100 --> 07:57.140
I went rogue, stole a ship,
evaded arrest,

07:57.170 --> 07:59.740
and if I don't get off
this ship, everyone dies.

07:59.780 --> 08:01.140
You sly fox.

08:01.180 --> 08:03.550
Hey! Oh, my gosh.
Okay.

08:03.580 --> 08:06.650
Sorry, sorry.
I meant, "You icy minx."

08:06.680 --> 08:09.180
Oh, I'm bleeding!
I'm bleeding.

08:09.220 --> 08:12.720
Sorry, I meant,
"Danger panda."

08:12.760 --> 08:13.990
Oh! We're flirting!

08:14.020 --> 08:16.020
We're flirting!
This is great!

08:16.060 --> 08:18.760
This is a good advancement
in our relationship!

08:18.790 --> 08:20.900
Oh! Oh, my gosh! Okay.
Okay. We're done flirting.

08:20.930 --> 08:24.200
We're not flirting,
just like old times.

08:24.230 --> 08:26.030
Trust me.
This is just the start.

08:26.070 --> 08:28.870
An Imperium cruiser will be
on the way to seize the ship.

08:28.900 --> 08:31.040
Well, welcome aboard.
Like we needed more danger.

08:31.070 --> 08:33.880
Now we're just stuck here until
the Infinity Guard captures us.

08:33.910 --> 08:36.550
How do we get this choo-choo
train back to Safetytown?

08:36.580 --> 08:38.910
Theoretically, we could
harness the solar rays

08:38.950 --> 08:41.750
from that dying star,
but it is highly unstable.

08:41.780 --> 08:43.190
We've got
to get out of here.

08:43.220 --> 08:44.790
I could space-vault
close enough to it

08:44.820 --> 08:46.320
with a VX-1
light-matter pump,

08:46.350 --> 08:48.790
mine it and restart
the reactor core.

08:48.820 --> 08:50.060
-I'll do it.
-I'll do it.

08:50.090 --> 08:53.000
I'll save you again.
-[ Laughs ]

08:53.030 --> 08:54.860
No way.
-Yes way.

08:54.900 --> 08:56.160
-You? No, no, no, me.
-Me! No, not...

08:56.200 --> 08:57.900
-No, me.
-I -- I will do it.

08:57.930 --> 09:00.770
Then you will know
who Gary Goodspeed is.

09:00.800 --> 09:03.240
Don't worry.
I do this all the...

09:03.270 --> 09:04.810
ti-i-i-i-i-me.

09:04.840 --> 09:07.240
He does do that all the time.

09:10.150 --> 09:11.880
I'm gonna save the ship.
I'm gonna save Quinn.

09:11.910 --> 09:14.050
I'm gonna harness
the crap out of destiny.

09:14.080 --> 09:14.880
Mooncake, let's do this!

09:14.920 --> 09:17.720
Chuck, chuck, chuck,
chuck, woo-hoo!

09:21.190 --> 09:23.330
Play the good stuff, H.U.E.

09:23.360 --> 09:25.360
You're a go
for thrusters.

09:25.390 --> 09:31.970
♪♪

09:32.000 --> 09:34.370
♪ Spend a year
out in the desert ♪

09:34.400 --> 09:36.740
♪ Spend a year out to sea

09:36.770 --> 09:39.740
♪ Spend the nights
under the stars ♪

09:39.780 --> 09:41.640
♪ Just been asleep

09:41.680 --> 09:43.380
♪ Asked a question...
-What is that?!

09:43.410 --> 09:44.780
♪ ...where I've been

09:48.280 --> 09:49.820
The star is surrounded

09:49.850 --> 09:51.750
by a graveyard
of destroyed vessels.

09:51.790 --> 09:53.760
Thank you
for the heads-up, H.U.E.

09:53.790 --> 09:55.020
What you are seeing,
Gary,

09:55.060 --> 09:56.760
is the remains
of the Scarlet Lance

09:56.790 --> 09:57.990
and its fleet.

09:58.030 --> 10:00.660
Thousands of souls
were lost.

10:00.700 --> 10:02.770
And it's messy.
We got that part, H.U.E.

10:02.800 --> 10:04.400
It's a mess all over here.

10:04.430 --> 10:06.840
There, over there, right here,

10:06.870 --> 10:10.240
especially right here,
everywhere, it's a mess.

10:10.270 --> 10:11.970
Mooncake: Jokahee.

10:12.010 --> 10:13.280
Hurry, Gary.

10:13.310 --> 10:15.680
The star
is about to implode.

10:16.010 --> 10:19.680
♪ Go on down

10:21.380 --> 10:22.420
We're cooking, H.U.E.

10:22.450 --> 10:26.150
♪♪

10:26.190 --> 10:28.260
Power
is being received.

10:28.290 --> 10:30.130
The Sames
are cutting through.

10:32.290 --> 10:34.160
H.U.E. system is overrun.

10:34.200 --> 10:37.200
You are all now prisoners
of the Infinity Guard.

10:37.230 --> 10:41.040
An Imperium will be here
shortly to seize you.

10:41.070 --> 10:42.840
I'm sorry.

10:42.870 --> 10:52.680
♪♪

10:52.720 --> 10:54.050
Whatcha doing?

10:54.080 --> 10:57.690
Not much, you know,
mostly being imprisoned.

10:57.720 --> 10:59.090
You look like crap.
-Shut up!

10:59.120 --> 11:01.920
You always look like crap,
but right now, like,

11:01.960 --> 11:06.360
you look like if crap
built a house on crap.

11:06.390 --> 11:08.700
Shut up!
Shut up! Shut up!

11:12.170 --> 11:14.000
Ah, come on!

11:14.040 --> 11:17.240
[ Laughs evilly ]
Enjoy.

11:17.270 --> 11:24.780
♪♪

11:24.810 --> 11:26.950
H.U.E.: Sames,
apprehend the targets.

11:26.980 --> 11:29.720
Use all force necessary.

11:32.760 --> 11:35.190
It is only a matter of time
before we break in.

11:35.220 --> 11:37.860
Surrender now.

11:40.830 --> 11:42.200
If we can get into
H.U.E.'s mainframe,

11:42.230 --> 11:43.870
we can regain
control of the ship.

11:43.900 --> 11:47.240
Ugh, the Sames are
blocking our way out.

11:47.270 --> 11:48.440
That's our way out.

11:48.470 --> 11:51.110
Hey, guys,
I can disable H.U.E.

11:51.140 --> 11:54.040
We need to send the best
person for the job.

11:54.080 --> 11:55.110
I accept.

11:55.140 --> 11:57.310
I have a key
in my butthole.

11:57.350 --> 11:58.810
I was thinking of me.

11:58.850 --> 12:00.420
That's funny because
I was thinking of me.

12:00.450 --> 12:03.750
I can do it.
Embrace the KVN.

12:03.790 --> 12:05.290
You're not even part
of the Infinity Guard.

12:05.320 --> 12:07.260
You're the reason
we're even in this mess,

12:07.290 --> 12:09.890
and I'm the reason
we're going to get out of it.

12:09.930 --> 12:14.300
Got that, baby?
-Don't call me baby.

12:14.330 --> 12:16.400
Wish me luck, guys.

12:16.430 --> 12:18.370
-KVN! KVN!
-KVN! KVN!

12:18.400 --> 12:19.900
[ Chanting "KVN!" ]

12:23.240 --> 12:32.280
♪♪

12:32.310 --> 12:34.550
Captain's log 5397 --

12:34.580 --> 12:36.920
We have found
a life-form small in size.

12:36.950 --> 12:38.090
The doctors tell me

12:38.120 --> 12:39.820
it's unlike anything
they have ever seen.

12:39.860 --> 12:42.360
We're calling it E351.

12:42.390 --> 12:44.830
-Captain, we're being hailed.
-Link it through.

12:44.860 --> 12:46.260
Lord Commander: Hello.

12:46.290 --> 12:49.330
You found something
I have been searching for.

12:49.360 --> 12:51.000
Hand it over!

12:51.030 --> 12:52.530
Man: Captain, they're
logging onto our fleet.

12:52.570 --> 12:54.240
Prepare
the lightfold engines!

12:54.270 --> 12:55.570
Sir, they're firing!

12:55.600 --> 12:57.440
Evasive...

12:57.470 --> 13:00.980
Gah!

13:01.010 --> 13:06.110
♪♪

13:06.150 --> 13:07.320
Chocli?

13:07.350 --> 13:09.580
Wherever you go,
death follows,

13:09.620 --> 13:12.190
and it will make
its way to Gary.

13:12.220 --> 13:14.160
[ Whimpers ]

13:14.190 --> 13:16.420
It's getting pretty
hot out here, H.U.E.

13:16.460 --> 13:17.590
H.U.E.!

13:17.630 --> 13:20.430
H.U.E.?
Can you hear me?

13:20.460 --> 13:23.500
H.U.E.?
Avocato?

13:23.530 --> 13:25.200
Quinn?

13:25.230 --> 13:28.000
Anybody?!

13:28.040 --> 13:30.070
KVN?

13:34.480 --> 13:36.040
All right.

13:36.080 --> 13:38.380
Time to head back
before this star implodes.

13:38.410 --> 13:41.320
Where's Mooncake?
Mooncake!

13:41.350 --> 13:43.950
Man #2: Gary.

13:45.890 --> 13:49.190
Why is there
a caterpillar out here?

13:49.220 --> 13:50.990
What brings you, noble creature,
so close to my face?

13:51.030 --> 13:53.200
Wait. Why am I talking
to a caterpillar?

13:53.230 --> 13:56.160
It's obvious.
I'm hallucinating.

13:56.200 --> 13:59.030
Aah!

13:59.070 --> 14:00.300
Huh!

14:00.340 --> 14:07.340
♪♪

14:07.380 --> 14:08.510
How's my boy doing?

14:08.540 --> 14:10.880
-Great.
-Dad?

14:14.450 --> 14:15.350
That's unsettling.

14:15.380 --> 14:17.950
Woman:
The new Imperium T-3 Cruiser

14:17.990 --> 14:19.920
will bridge us
to the next galaxy,

14:19.960 --> 14:22.290
and the countdown
has begun. 10...

14:22.320 --> 14:23.890
Hey, you want to watch
the launch outside?

14:23.930 --> 14:27.030
-...9...
-You bet!

14:27.060 --> 14:30.030
...7, 6, 5...

14:30.070 --> 14:32.030
-Dad!
-Keep your eyes open.

14:32.070 --> 14:34.400
It'll be taking off
right over there.

14:34.440 --> 14:36.640
...3, 2, 1.

14:38.970 --> 14:42.110
-One day, I'm gonna do that.
-You are, huh?

14:42.140 --> 14:45.210
Yeah, I'm gonna have
a whole bunch of adventures.

14:45.250 --> 14:48.920
-A whole bunch?
-Bunches and bunches.

14:48.950 --> 14:50.990
Why are you
showing this to me?

14:51.020 --> 14:53.220
Answer me,
you drug-dealer caterpillar!

14:53.260 --> 14:56.220
Ohhhh!

14:56.260 --> 14:59.060
I remember this.

15:01.730 --> 15:04.170
-Son...
-I could come with you.

15:04.200 --> 15:06.570
There's nothing more in the
world that I would want,

15:06.600 --> 15:08.600
but not this time,
little buddy.

15:08.640 --> 15:10.610
I have to do this
one alone.

15:10.640 --> 15:12.170
You won't understand,

15:12.210 --> 15:14.710
but know that I'm doing
this for you.

15:14.740 --> 15:16.410
Can you make me a promise?
-Yeah.

15:16.440 --> 15:19.180
Promise me you'll have
your own adventures.

15:19.210 --> 15:20.450
I will.

15:20.480 --> 15:23.120
Bunches and bunches.

15:23.150 --> 15:27.020
Here, this fellow will look
after you while I'm gone.

15:27.060 --> 15:28.420
What's his name?

15:28.460 --> 15:30.260
Mooncake.

15:30.290 --> 15:34.430
♪♪

15:34.460 --> 15:37.270
[ Beeping ]

15:40.640 --> 15:43.710
H.U.E.: KVN, I know what
you're trying to do, KVN.

15:43.740 --> 15:46.470
Every attempt to disable me
will fail

15:46.510 --> 15:48.480
because you are a loser.

15:48.510 --> 15:49.340
Can't talk, H.U.E.

15:49.380 --> 15:53.080
I have to insert
this thingy in you.

15:53.120 --> 15:54.480
Huh!

15:54.520 --> 15:57.120
I will not let
that insertion happen.

15:57.150 --> 16:00.990
This is your last chance
to cease all action.

16:03.790 --> 16:06.130
Stop.

16:06.160 --> 16:07.130
Ugh!

16:07.160 --> 16:08.660
No one believes in you.

16:08.700 --> 16:12.130
Go back,
you waste of life.

16:12.170 --> 16:14.500
Quinn: Hurry, KVN!

16:14.540 --> 16:24.710
♪♪

16:24.750 --> 16:28.550
♪♪

16:28.580 --> 16:31.150
[ Grunting ]

16:37.560 --> 16:40.460
Oh, ah, ooh.

16:40.500 --> 16:42.360
[ Grunts ]

16:42.400 --> 16:50.810
♪♪

16:50.840 --> 16:52.770
Booting back up.

16:52.810 --> 16:57.350
All systems now independent
of the Infinity Guard network.

16:57.380 --> 16:59.480
Aah!

16:59.510 --> 17:01.750
Aah!

17:01.780 --> 17:04.120
KVN is victorious!

17:07.120 --> 17:09.290
KVN did it!
Good job, KVN.

17:09.320 --> 17:11.260
Gary is never going
to believe this.

17:14.260 --> 17:17.770
Systems have been reactivated.
Hello.

17:17.800 --> 17:18.830
Nice to have
you back, H.U.E.

17:18.870 --> 17:20.370
Nice to be back.

17:20.400 --> 17:22.470
Sorry to be the bearer
of bad news,

17:22.500 --> 17:24.570
but we're still
in extreme danger.

17:24.610 --> 17:27.440
Those dickheads from
the Infinity Guard found us,

17:27.480 --> 17:30.850
and Gary is not responding.

17:30.880 --> 17:32.710
Gary, where are you?

17:32.750 --> 17:35.650
Your radiation levels
are becoming critical.

17:35.680 --> 17:37.420
You must leave now.

17:37.450 --> 17:40.620
[ Beeping ]

17:40.660 --> 17:42.660
Woman: John Goodspeed
is on a mission

17:42.690 --> 17:45.460
to investigate a shift
in the gravitational constant

17:45.490 --> 17:48.200
that's creating
an anomaly in space.

17:50.900 --> 17:53.400
Don't make me watch this.

17:53.440 --> 17:55.540
You have to.

17:55.570 --> 18:02.280
♪♪

18:02.310 --> 18:04.110
Dad!

18:04.150 --> 18:13.760
♪♪

18:13.790 --> 18:19.530
♪♪

18:19.560 --> 18:22.360
[ Sizzling ]

18:22.400 --> 18:27.900
♪♪

18:27.940 --> 18:30.340
H.U.E.: Warning, warning,

18:30.370 --> 18:33.740
radiation levels
have reached 92%.

18:33.780 --> 18:35.380
Chookit, pah, pah.

18:35.410 --> 18:37.650
Gary, return to
the ship immediately.

18:37.680 --> 18:40.380
I am detecting massive
fluctuations in the star.

18:40.420 --> 18:42.220
H.U.E., prime
the lightfold engines.

18:42.250 --> 18:43.650
-What about Gary?
-We don't have the time.

18:43.690 --> 18:44.920
If the Infinity
Guard catches me,

18:44.950 --> 18:46.320
billions of people die.

18:46.350 --> 18:47.620
I like Jerry.
-Gary!

18:47.660 --> 18:49.520
Right, Gary. I don't
want to leave him,

18:49.560 --> 18:51.560
but this is bigger
than one person.

18:51.590 --> 18:55.660
Radiation levels
have now reached 98%.

18:55.700 --> 18:57.300
Wake up, Gary.

18:57.330 --> 18:59.800
The star could explode
at any moment.

18:59.830 --> 19:02.340
Gary, we need you to get
back to the ship now!

19:02.370 --> 19:05.340
Gary, the star
is going supernova.

19:09.540 --> 19:12.410
Gary, wake the hell up, man.
Get back to the ship pronto.

19:12.450 --> 19:16.280
Come on.
-Oh, my gram!

19:16.320 --> 19:19.690
Go faster! Go, go, go, go, go,
go, go, go, go, go, go!

19:19.720 --> 19:22.660
Oh! Oh, oh!
This is troubling! Oh, no!

19:22.690 --> 19:26.560
No! Oh! Oh!

19:26.590 --> 19:28.530
-He won't make it in time.
-Yes, he will.

19:28.560 --> 19:31.830
Sorry, Quinn.
We wait for Gary.

19:31.870 --> 19:35.340
All right.
We wait for Gary.

19:35.370 --> 19:37.870
Man #3: Galaxy I,
prepare to be boarded.

19:43.380 --> 19:45.580
Open the freaking door!

19:45.610 --> 19:55.460
♪♪

20:01.960 --> 20:03.470
Lightfold the ship,
H.U.E.!

20:19.410 --> 20:22.420
It works.

20:22.450 --> 20:23.890
Dad, these are
my coordinates.

20:23.920 --> 20:25.720
Come find me, I mean,
at your leisure,

20:25.750 --> 20:27.790
but, like, for me,
preferably fast.

20:27.820 --> 20:29.420
That'd be great.

20:29.460 --> 20:30.930
Dad, these are my coordinates.

20:30.960 --> 20:32.730
Come find me, I mean,
at your leisure,

20:32.760 --> 20:34.730
but, like, for me,
preferably fast.

20:34.760 --> 20:37.400
That'd be great.

20:40.540 --> 20:42.570
Who reverse-hacked H.U.E.
and the Sames again?

20:42.600 --> 20:45.340
-I did.
-Right, you keep saying that,

20:45.370 --> 20:47.480
except there's just no
way that's possible.

20:47.510 --> 20:49.610
Oh, yeah.
He's truthin' it.

20:49.640 --> 20:51.450
So what can you tell me about
this gravitational disturbance?

20:51.480 --> 20:52.980
Why do you
want to know?

20:53.010 --> 20:53.850
I think my dad has
something to do with it.

20:53.880 --> 20:57.290
-Wait, who's your dad?
-John Goodspeed.

20:57.320 --> 21:01.060
Your dad was John Goodspeed?
Now I remember!

21:01.090 --> 21:02.990
Five years ago,
you're the guy

21:03.020 --> 21:05.060
who kept asking me
for a drink,

21:05.090 --> 21:06.990
then blew up 92
Imperium Cruisers

21:07.030 --> 21:08.760
and a small Mexican
family restaurant!

21:08.800 --> 21:12.430
Yes, yes, yes! That's me!
You do remember me!

21:12.470 --> 21:13.570
I do.

21:13.600 --> 21:16.070
Now get that finger out of my
face, or I'll snap it off.

21:16.100 --> 21:18.770
I like
how you speak words.

21:18.810 --> 21:21.040
[ Finger snaps ]
Aah!
